        },
        {
          "title": "FINDINGS OF FACT",
          "elements": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "list_type": "ordered",
              "items": [
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "text": "The Respondent’s Division of Medical Assistance (“DMA”) administers and manages \nNorth Carolina’s Medicaid Plan and Program. Pursuant to N.C. Gen. Stat. § 108A-54, \nDMA is authorized to adopt rules, regulations, and policies for program operation.",
                      "bold": false,
                      "italic": false,
                      "underline": false,
                      "strikethrough": false,
                      "superscript": false,
                      "subscript": false,
                      "code": false,
                      "lang": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "nested_list": null,
                  "term": null,
                  "definition": null
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "text": "At all times pertinent hereto, Petitioner was an enrolled dental provider in the North \nCarolina Medicaid Program and entered into a Medicaid Participation Agreement with \nDMA as part of its enrollment. (Respondent’s Ex. 1, hereinafter, “R Ex 1.”)",
                      "bold": false,
                      "italic": false,
                      "underline": false,
                      "strikethrough": false,
                      "superscript": false,
                      "subscript": false,
                      "code": false,
                      "lang": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "nested_list": null,
                  "term": null,
                  "definition": null
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "text": "By entering into the Medicaid Participation Agreement, Petitioner agreed to “comply \nwith all [F]ederal and [S]tate laws, regulations, and rules, State Medicaid Plan, and \npolicies, provider manuals, and Medicaid bulletins published by [DMA] and/or its \nfiscal agent in effect at the time the service is rendered,” and to “submit claims for \nservices rendered to eligible beneficiaries, as identified by [DMA], in accordance with \nrules and billing instructions in effect at the time the service is rendered.” (R Ex 1, p. \n5.)",
                      "bold": false,
                      "italic": false,
                      "underline": false,
                      "strikethrough": false,
                      "superscript": false,
                      "subscript": false,
                      "code": false,
                      "lang": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "nested_list": null,
                  "term": null,
                  "definition": null
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "text": "Petitioner and its principal, Dr. James A. Harrold, participated in the North Carolina \nMedicaid for Pregnant Women program (“MPW”) as a service to the community, \naccepting the substantially lower reimbursement for dental services provided by the \nMedicaid fee schedule. ",
                      "bold": false,
                      "italic": false,
                      "underline": false,
                      "strikethrough": false,
                      "superscript": false,
                      "subscript": false,
                      "code": false,
                      "lang": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "nested_list": null,
                  "term": null,
                  "definition": null
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "text": "Medicaid recipients in some eligibility categories were ineligible for dental services. \nPregnant Medicaid eligible recipients covered under the Medicaid for Pregnant Women \nprogram were identified with the code “MPWN” in online Medicaid records that \nparticipating dental practices could access, and prior to 2009, received a pink Medicaid \nidentification card. ",
                      "bold": false,
                      "italic": false,
                      "underline": false,
                      "strikethrough": false,
                      "superscript": false,
                      "subscript": false,
                      "code": false,
                      "lang": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "nested_list": null,
                  "term": null,
                  "definition": null
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "text": "Beneficiaries in the MPW program received gynecological, screening, diagnostic and \ntreatment services during pregnancy and postpartum. Typically, recipients were \nfollowed for two or three months following delivery, but for much longer periods if \nthere were complications resulting from the pregnancy or delivery. ",
                      "bold": false,
                      "italic": false,
                      "underline": false,
                      "strikethrough": false,
                      "superscript": false,
                      "subscript": false,
                      "code": false,
                      "lang": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "nested_list": null,
                  "term": null,
                  "definition": null
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "text": "Unlike medical and allied health services, the MPW beneficiaries’ eligibility for dental \nservices terminated on “the day of delivery.” (R Ex 6, p. 8.) However, the online \ninformation that the participating dental practices could access did not reflect any \nchange in MPW beneficiaries’ status following delivery.",
                      "bold": false,
                      "italic": false,
                      "underline": false,
                      "strikethrough": false,
                      "superscript": false,
                      "subscript": false,
                      "code": false,
                      "lang": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "nested_list": null,
                  "term": null,
                  "definition": null
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "text": "As a practical matter, Petitioner’s staff frequently could not rely on visual contact with \nMPW beneficiaries when they arrived at their dental office to determine if they were \npregnant. Consequently, Petitioner’s staff routinely inquired of MPW beneficiaries, on \neach visit, whether they were pregnant. When they were told or were otherwise made \naware that a MPW beneficiary was not pregnant, Petitioner’s staff did not bill \nMedicaid.",
                      "bold": false,
                      "italic": false,
                      "underline": false,
                      "strikethrough": false,
                      "superscript": false,
                      "subscript": false,
                      "code": false,
                      "lang": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "nested_list": null,
                  "term": null,
                  "definition": null
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "text": "The Respondent purposefully and designedly blocked dental practices participating in \nthe MPW program, along with the general public, from accessing Medicaid’s online \nrecords of gynecological and other medical services rendered to MPW beneficiaries \nwhich would have aided them in determining whether those patients remained eligible \nfor dental services. As a foreseeable and known consequence, Petitioner was impelled \nto rely upon the statements of MPW beneficiaries in some instances to determine their \neligibility for dental services under the MPW program. The ",
                      "bold": false,
                      "italic": false,
                      "underline": false,
                      "strikethrough": false,
                      "superscript": false,
                      "subscript": false,
                      "code": false,
                      "lang": null
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Basic Medicaid Billing \nGuide",
                      "bold": false,
                      "italic": true,
                      "underline": false,
                      "strikethrough": false,
                      "superscript": false,
                      "subscript": false,
                      "code": false,
                      "lang": null
                    },
                    {
                      "text": " instructed providers to question patients when their eligibility could not \notherwise be determined. (R Ex 7, p. 2-13.)",
                      "bold": false,
                      "italic": false,
                      "underline": false,
                      "strikethrough": false,
                      "superscript": false,
                      "subscript": false,
                      "code": false,
                      "lang": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "nested_list": null,
                  "term": null,
                  "definition": null
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "text": "By 2014, improvements in the computer programs handling the State’s Medicaid \nrecords made it relatively easy for the Respondent’s Program Integrity Unit to query \nthis data and compare the dates when services were rendered for MPW beneficiaries. ",
                      "bold": false,
                      "italic": false,
                      "underline": false,
                      "strikethrough": false,
                      "superscript": false,
                      "subscript": false,
                      "code": false,
                      "lang": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "nested_list": null,
                  "term": null,
                  "definition": null
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "text": "In December 2014, Respondent notified Petitioner that a post payment review had \n“revealed program abuse,” evidenced by data showing that 19 MPW beneficiaries \nduring the period January 15, 2009 through June 11, 2012 had received some dental \nservices from Petitioner on dates established to be after their pregnancy, in one instance \nby two days. (R Ex 2; R Ex 3, p. 1.) ",
                      "bold": false,
                      "italic": false,
                      "underline": false,
                      "strikethrough": false,
                      "superscript": false,
                      "subscript": false,
                      "code": false,
                      "lang": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "nested_list": null,
                  "term": null,
                  "definition": null
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "text": "Petitioner’s Administrator testified that their records concerning these 19 patients were \nreviewed following Respondent’s notice. It was discovered in the file of the third \npatient listed in Respondent’s Exhibit 3 that the fact that she was no longer pregnant \nhad been noted, but that Petitioner had mistakenly billed Medicaid $1,073.45 for this \nMPW beneficiary’s treatment.",
                      "bold": false,
                      "italic": false,
                      "underline": false,
                      "strikethrough": false,
                      "superscript": false,
                      "subscript": false,
                      "code": false,
                      "lang": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "nested_list": null,
                  "term": null,
                  "definition": null
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "text": "As a part of Petitioner’s agreement with DMA, Petitioner agreed “[t]o refund or allow \nthe Department to recoup or recover any monies received in error or in excess of the \namount to which the provider is entitled ... regardless of whether the error was caused \nby the provider or the Department and/or its agents.” (R Ex 1, “Provider Enrollment \nForm,” p. 6 of 9.)",
                      "bold": false,
                      "italic": false,
                      "underline": false,
                      "strikethrough": false,
                      "superscript": false,
                      "subscript": false,
                      "code": false,
                      "lang": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "nested_list": null,
                  "term": null,
                  "definition": null
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "text": "There is no evidence that any other payment to Petitioner for these services actually \nrendered was the result of a mistake by either party, or due to any violation of or \ndeviation from any law, regulation, rule, policy, provider manual, Medicaid bulletin, \nor the State Medicaid Plan.",
                      "bold": false,
                      "italic": false,
                      "underline": false,
                      "strikethrough": false,
                      "superscript": false,
                      "subscript": false,
                      "code": false,
                      "lang": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "nested_list": null,
                  "term": null,
                  "definition": null
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "text": "Petitioner timely filed a request for a contested case hearing in the Office of \nAdministrative Hearings. See, ",
                      "bold": false,
                      "italic": false,
                      "underline": false,
                      "strikethrough": false,
                      "superscript": false,
                      "subscript": false,
                      "code": false,
                      "lang": null
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Order Denying Motion to Dismiss",
                      "bold": false,
                      "italic": true,
                      "underline": false,
                      "strikethrough": false,
                      "superscript": false,
                      "subscript": false,
                      "code": false,
                      "lang": null
                    },
                    {
                      "text": ", filed July 17, 2015.",
                      "bold": false,
                      "italic": false,
                      "underline": false,
                      "strikethrough": false,
                      "superscript": false,
                      "subscript": false,
                      "code": false,
                      "lang": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "nested_list": null,
                  "term": null,
                  "definition": null
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "text": "The Office of Administrative Hearings has personal and subject matter jurisdiction over \nthis contested case. The parties received proper notice of the hearing. ",
                      "bold": false,
                      "italic": false,
                      "underline": false,
                      "strikethrough": false,
                      "superscript": false,
                      "subscript": false,
                      "code": false,
                      "lang": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "nested_list": null,
                  "term": null,
                  "definition": null
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "text": "To the extent that the foregoing Findings of Fact contain conclusions of law, or that \nthese Conclusions of Law are findings of fact, they should be so considered without \nregard to their given labels. ",
                      "bold": false,
                      "italic": false,
                      "underline": false,
                      "strikethrough": false,
                      "superscript": false,
                      "subscript": false,
                      "code": false,
                      "lang": null
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Charlotte v. Heath",
                      "bold": false,
                      "italic": true,
                      "underline": false,
                      "strikethrough": false,
                      "superscript": false,
                      "subscript": false,
                      "code": false,
                      "lang": null
                    },
                    {
                      "text": ", 226 N.C. 750, 755, 40 S.E.2d 600, 604 \n(1946); ",
                      "bold": false,
                      "italic": false,
                      "underline": false,
                      "strikethrough": false,
                      "superscript": false,
                      "subscript": false,
                      "code": false,
                      "lang": null
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Peters v. Pennington",
                      "bold": false,
                      "italic": true,
                      "underline": false,
                      "strikethrough": false,
                      "superscript": false,
                      "subscript": false,
                      "code": false,
                      "lang": null
                    },
                    {
                      "text": ", 210 N.C. App. 1, 15, 707 S.E.2d 724, 735 (2011).",
                      "bold": false,
                      "italic": false,
                      "underline": false,
                      "strikethrough": false,
                      "superscript": false,
                      "subscript": false,
                      "code": false,
                      "lang": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "nested_list": null,
                  "term": null,
                  "definition": null
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "text": "Petitioner bears the burden of proof in this appeal of an adverse determination by the \nRespondent to seek to recoup a Medicaid payment. N.C. Gen. Stat. §§ 108C-2(1); \n108C-12(d).",
                      "bold": false,
                      "italic": false,
                      "underline": false,
                      "strikethrough": false,
                      "superscript": false,
                      "subscript": false,
                      "code": false,
                      "lang": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "nested_list": null,
                  "term": null,
                  "definition": null
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "text": "The uncontroverted evidence shows that Respondent is entitled to recoup $1,073.45.",
                      "bold": false,
                      "italic": false,
                      "underline": false,
                      "strikethrough": false,
                      "superscript": false,
                      "subscript": false,
                      "code": false,
                      "lang": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "nested_list": null,
                  "term": null,
                  "definition": null
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "text": "Petitioner met its burden of showing by a preponderance of the evidence that it has not \notherwise received funds in contravention of its agreement with the Respondent.",
                      "bold": false,
                      "italic": false,
                      "underline": false,
                      "strikethrough": false,
                      "superscript": false,
                      "subscript": false,
                      "code": false,
                      "lang": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "nested_list": null,
                  "term": null,
                  "definition": null
                }
              ],
              "reading_order": null
            }
          ],
          "reading_order": 7,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "title": "CONCLUSIONS OF LAW",
          "elements": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Based upon the foregoing Findings of Fact and Conclusions of Law, the undersigned makes \nthe following: ",
                  "bold": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "underline": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "superscript": false,
                  "subscript": false,
                  "code": false,
                  "lang": null
                }
              ],
              "lang": null,
              "reading_order": null
            }
          ],
          "reading_order": 8,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "title": "DECISION",
          "elements": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "IT IS ORDERED ",
                  "bold": true,
                  "italic": false,
                  "underline": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "superscript": false,
                  "subscript": false,
                  "code": false,
                  "lang": null
                },
                {
                  "text": "that the Petitioner shall pay over to the Respondent Department of \nHealth and Human Services, Division of Medical Assistance to sum of ONE THOUSAND \nSEVENTY-THREE and 45/100 DOLLARS ($1,073.45). ",
                  "bold": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "underline": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "superscript": false,
                  "subscript": false,
                  "code": false,
                  "lang": null
                }
              ],
              "lang": null,
