            }
          ],
          "reading_order": 9,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "title": "NOTICE",
          "elements": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "This is a Final Decision ",
                  "bold": true,
                  "italic": false,
                  "underline": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "superscript": false,
                  "subscript": false,
                  "code": false,
                  "lang": null
                },
                {
                  "text": "issued under the authority of N.C. Gen. Stat. § 150B-34.",
                  "bold": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "underline": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "superscript": false,
                  "subscript": false,
                  "code": false,
                  "lang": null
                }
              ],
              "lang": null,
              "reading_order": null
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Under the provisions of North Carolina General Statute § 150B-45, any party wishing to \nappeal the final decision of the Administrative Law Judge must file a Petition for Judicial Review \nin the Superior Court of the county where the person aggrieved by the administrative decision \nresides, or in the case of a person residing outside the State, the county where the contested case \nwhich resulted in the final decision was filed. ",
                  "bold": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "underline": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "superscript": false,
                  "subscript": false,
                  "code": false,
                  "lang": null
                },
                {
                  "text": "The appealing party must file the petition within \n30 days after being served with a written copy of the Administrative Law Judge’s Final \nDecision",
                  "bold": true,
                  "italic": false,
                  "underline": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "superscript": false,
                  "subscript": false,
                  "code": false,
                  "lang": null
                },
                {
                  "text": ". In conformity with the Office of Administrative Hearings’ rule, 26 N.C. Admin. Code \n03.0102, and the Rules of Civil Procedure, N.C. General Statute 1A-1, Article 2, ",
                  "bold": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "underline": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "superscript": false,
                  "subscript": false,
                  "code": false,
                  "lang": null
                },
                {
                  "text": "this Final \nDecision was served on the parties the date it was placed in the mail as indicated by the date \non the Certificate of Service attached to this Final Decision",
                  "bold": true,
                  "italic": false,
                  "underline": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "superscript": false,
                  "subscript": false,
                  "code": false,
                  "lang": null
                },
                {
                  "text": ". N.C. Gen. Stat. § 150B-46 \ndescribes the contents of the Petition and requires service of the Petition on all parties. Under N.C. \nGen. Stat. § 150B-47, the Office of Administrative Hearings is required to file the official record \nin the contested case with the Clerk of Superior Court within 30 days of receipt of the Petition for \nJudicial Review. Consequently, a copy of the Petition for Judicial Review must be sent to the \nOffice of Administrative Hearings at the time the appeal is initiated in order to ensure the timely \nfiling of the record.",
                  "bold": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "underline": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "superscript": false,
                  "subscript": false,
                  "code": false,
                  "lang": null
                }
              ],
              "lang": null,
              "reading_order": null
            },
            {
